+
+- **P1 — Timeline moves information required to interpret the visible rows.** When all events share one year, the rows deliberately omit it because it is stated once above the list ([TimelinePanel.tsx](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/TimelinePanel.tsx:120), [TimelinePanel.tsx](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/TimelinePanel.tsx:339)). Hiding “Everything dated here is in 2026” makes dates such as “12 May” ambiguous. Likewise, the thin-timeline note is a substantive qualification: the code says readers cannot infer it from the rows ([TimelinePanel.tsx](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/TimelinePanel.tsx:75)). Keep both visible; only move count and provenance. This contradicts the table at [plan:88](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/docs/plans/261001m-every-mode-gets-an-i-in-its-top-right-corner.md:88).
+
+- **P1 — The clearance design needs explicit treatment for scroller-first and measured modes.** Outline requires the visible list and hidden candidates to have exactly the same width ([outline-mode.css](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/styles/outline-mode.css:40), [outline-mode.css](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/styles/outline-mode.css:340)); padding only the visible “top row” can select a rung that later overflows. Adjust `--outln-pad-r` so both copies share the inset. Also give the corner button an explicit stacking level above sticky content—Ideas’ first heading is `z-index: 1` ([ideas.css](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/styles/ideas.css:60)). The absolute approach itself is fine and does not consume Search’s zero slack, but [plan:47-50](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/docs/plans/261001m-every-mode-gets-an-i-in-its-top-right-corner.md:47) should inventory the actual clearance selector for every scroller-first/measured face.
+
+- **P1 — The rename has already corrupted historical evidence.** Greg’s quoted wording says `new-mode.md` ([plan:11-14](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/docs/plans/261001m-every-mode-gets-an-i-in-its-top-right-corner.md:11)), but the renamed doc now quotes him as saying `mode.md` ([mode.md](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/docs/project/mode.md:149)), contrary to the exact-quote rule ([documentation-policy.md](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/docs/reusable/documentation-policy.md:67)). Recorded review `.diff` files were rewritten too. Update live links and references, but preserve quotations, code fences/diffs, prompts, and historical prose. This is the concrete risk in [plan:107-110](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/docs/plans/261001m-every-mode-gets-an-i-in-its-top-right-corner.md:107).
+
+- **P2 — The guard is total over modes, but not over the states promised.** Phase B explicitly mounts only each owner’s populated fixture ([every-mode-draws-its-surface.test.tsx](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/tests/every-mode-draws-its-surface.test.tsx:1281)). It will go red and prevents a new populated owner mode from omitting the icon, but it cannot catch an `about={artefact && …}` that removes the icon while loading, empty, or visiting. Assert exactly one direct, first-child `.band-about`, add a focused `ModeSurface` test, and cover representative empty and visitor states.
+
+- **P2 — Three table entries need adjustment.** Debate’s order sentence should stay beside the order control: its own comment says it must be seen before reading the list ([DebatePanel.tsx](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/DebatePanel.tsx:1199)). FAQ should add `questions.length` to its card; its only current count exists in the prioritised threshold ([FaqPanel.tsx](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/FaqPanel.tsx:353)). Referee is not already the requested corner `(i)`: it is deliberately a textual button ([referee.css](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/web/styles/referee.css:365)). Preserve its large inline card, but use the standard corner icon as its trigger, or call out that product exception for approval.
+
+- **P2 — Reuse the existing static mode copy.** `MODE_CATALOG.description` and `.how` already own “what this mode is” and are exhaustive specifically to prevent per-mode copy drifting ([mode-catalog.ts](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/mode-catalog.ts:1), [mode-catalog.ts](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb8h-mode-info-icon/src/mode-catalog.ts:77)). Use those for the card’s opening paragraphs, then append dynamic counts, caveats, and `AboutMade`.
+
+Verdict: **revise, then build**. Absolute positioning, first focus position, and the existing tooltip accessibility mechanics are sound; the blockers are the Timeline regression, incomplete clearance contract, and rename damage.
